//
// Documentation for Kitsune-specific global variable attributes. This is used
// to generate an HTML page with the documentation.
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

def GlobalDocumentation {
  code Intro =[{..
  -------------------------------------------------------------------
  NOTE: This file is automatically generated by running llvm-tblgen
  -gen-kit-func-attr-doc. Do not edit this file by hand!!
  -------------------------------------------------------------------

========================================
LLVM Global Variable Attribute Reference
========================================
.. contents::
  :local:

.. |br| raw:: html

  <br/>

These are Kitsune-specific attributes that may be attached to global variables.
These attributes must be one of the following kinds.

* **Flag Attributes**: These are attributes that do not take a value. Only
  their presence or absence is significant.

* **Valued Attributes**: These are attributes that take a value. Currently,
  only certain types of values are supported. These, together with the
  corresponding type that will appear in the LLVM-IR metadata are
  summarized in the table below.

  =============  ============
  Source type    LLVM-IR type
  =============  ============
  ``int32_t``    ``i32``
  ``int64_t``    ``i64``
  ``StringRef``  ``[n x i8]``
  =============  ============

* **Enum Attributes**: These are a special case of the valued attributes
  where the value type is an **enum** defined in Kitsune's source. The
  type of the value in LLVM-IR metadata will always be ``i32``.

In the example below, a flag attribute has been added to global variable `g`.
:ref:`kit.gv.bit.code <gv-attr-bit-code>`, and
:ref:`kit.gv.kernel.properties <gv-attr-kernel-properties>`.

.. code :: kitll

  @g = external global i32, !kit.gv.bit.code !0, !kit.gv.kernel.properties !1

  !0 = !{i32 2}
  !1 = !{!"kernel_func"}

Every attribute has an entry in the ``GVAttrKind`` enum.
}];
}

include "kitsune/Core/GVAttrs.td"
